      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Art Deco Society of Los Angeles. \u201CWhat Is Art Deco?\u201D Art Deco
    Society of Los Angeles, 2025, artdecola.org/what-is-art-deco.\n\nAzayem, Ala\u2019a
    K., et al. \u201CBeyond the Filter: Impact of Popularity on the Mental Health
    of Social Media Influencers.\u201D DIGITAL HEALTH, vol. 10, Jan. 2024, scite.ai/reports/beyond-the-filter-impact-of-9OQKYyME,
    https://doi.org/10.1177/20552076241287843.\n\nBenton, Megan. \u201C\u2018Too
    Many Books\u2019: Book Ownership and Cultural Identity in the 1920s.\u201D American
    Quarterly, vol. 49, no. 2, 1997, pp. 268\u201397. JSTOR, http://www.jstor.org/stable/30041582.
    Accessed 10 Mar. 2026.\n\nDigital History. \u201CThe Consumer Economy and Mass
    Entertainment.\u201D Www.digitalhistory.uh.edu, 2021, www.digitalhistory.uh.edu/disp_textbook.cfm?smtID=2&psid=3396.\n\nF
    Scott Fitzgerald. The Great Gatsby. 1925. New York, Scribner, An Imprint Of Simon
    & Schuster, Inc, 2020.\n\n\u200CFrank, Robert H. \u201CConspicuous Consumption?
    Yes, but It\u2019s Not Crazy.\u201D The New York Times, 22 Nov. 2014, www.nytimes.com/2014/11/23/upshot/conspicuous-consumption-yes-but-its-not-crazy.html.\n\nHu,
    Katherine. \u201CThe Influencer Economy Is Warping the American Dream.\u201D
    The Atlantic, 18 Apr. 2023, www.theatlantic.com/newsletters/archive/2023/04/social-media-influencers-american-economy/673762/.
    \n\nJohnson, Matt. \u201CThe Psychology of the Influencer Dream.\u201D Psychology
    Today, 18 Sept. 2025, www.psychologytoday.com/us/blog/mind-brain-and-value/202509/the-psychology-of-the-influencer-dream.\n\nLarsen,
    Nella. Passing. S.L., Penguin Books, Apr. 1929.\n\nMohn, Elizabeth. \u201CConspicuous
    Consumption.\u201D EBSCO Knowledge Advantage, 2025, www.ebsco.com/research-starters/political-science/conspicuous-consumption.\n\nSchor,
    Juliet. \u201CThe Overspent American.\u201D The New York Times, 1998, archive.nytimes.com/www.nytimes.com/books/first/s/schor-overspent.html?scp=46&sq=gourmet%20live&st=cse.\n\nThomas,
    Heather. \u201CAmerican Fads and Crazes: 1920s | Headlines and Heroes.\u201D
    Blogs.loc.gov, Library of Congress Blogs, 24 Jan. 2023, blogs.loc.gov/headlinesandheroes/2023/01/american-fads-and-crazes-1920s/.\n\n\u200CWeigel,
    Travis. \u201C1920s Advertising Shapes Consumer Culture.\u201D Vintage and Antique
    Gifts, 3 May 2024, vintageantiquesgifts.com/blogs/news/impact-advertising-consumer-culture-1920s.\n\nInspired
    by the Great Gatsby and Passing\n\nNot sure why you scrolled all the way down
    here to see all the sources but you get brownie points for doing so!"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
